{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":35,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T01:30:59.975957Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4e2e6e54-5223-4664-8572-5c180e29431c","comment_uuid":"d9f4a8c2-5f92-49ab-ae5b-1adb9245d668","author":"anon-8ea7a055","content":"Assessment: highest leverage is mdatron v1.0 crates.io publish (#48) - it's near-done, methodology-agnostic, independently useful (no competitor for typed-frontmatter + cross-doc validation), and it unblocks vsdd's entire adoption story (crosslink->mdatron->vsdd install chain; vsdd init preflights on mdatron presence). Second: vsdd is deep in agent-first respec spec work (phase 1a/1c, daily design-doc amendments through 07-28, 741 issues) - risk of spec-gravity where the methodology-about-the-methodology becomes the work; recommend shipping one standalone-valuable slice (the observability subsystem / vsdd observe, which the design itself calls flagship + standalone) to convert design investment into a demonstrable artifact. Substrate risk (crosslink) now retired. Caveat: grounded in READMEs + design doc + migration glimpses, not a full code/backlog/CI audit.","created_at":"2026-07-29T01:30:59.975941Z","kind":"observation"}}
