{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":67,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T06:59:14.613076Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"a3abff8a-7d9a-44fe-9a11-8e75a232d612","title":"Fix dashboard serve crash on static assets (forecast-bio#654, unmigrated); refile on dollspace","priority":"high","created_by":"anon-8ea7a055"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":68,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T06:59:19.341541Z","event":{"type":"LabelAdded","issue_uuid":"a3abff8a-7d9a-44fe-9a11-8e75a232d612","label":"bug"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":69,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T07:05:21.257787Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"a3abff8a-7d9a-44fe-9a11-8e75a232d612","comment_uuid":"2626c482-0b00-4954-a1a0-491d0a251e62","author":"anon-8ea7a055","content":"Repro investigation on develop (d77a37ba): (1) serve/embedded code is BYTE-IDENTICAL to the beta tag 7854152b the bug was filed against (verified git diff) - so it's not an already-landed source fix. (2) --dashboard-dir (ServeDir) path does NOT crash: serves a 33-byte JS AND an 800KB JS with 200, server stays alive. (3) serve_embedded (the embedded path) is panic-safe by inspection - Response::builder().body().unwrap_or_else(500), no panicking unwrap; Option-guarded gets. (4) Router has NO layers; mod.rs layers (auth_middleware, DefaultBodyLimit, CORS) are all panic-safe and shared with the working ServeDir path. Strong hypothesis: does NOT reproduce on develop (likely a beta-build/environment or Cargo.lock-specific issue at release time). Building real frontend + embedded binary now to test the embedded path definitively before concluding.","created_at":"2026-07-29T07:05:21.257765Z","kind":"observation"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":70,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T07:17:08.533223Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"a3abff8a-7d9a-44fe-9a11-8e75a232d612","comment_uuid":"e1e5cb80-e1a4-4ccb-b1a2-427e8b99363d","author":"anon-8ea7a055","content":"DEFINITIVE: fb#654 does NOT reproduce on develop. Built an embedded release binary with a real 533KB JS asset baked in, ran 'crosslink dashboard serve' (embedded path, the issue's exact repro), curled /assets/index-COsZ_-s7.js -> 200 text/javascript 533KB, server stayed ALIVE. No crash on EITHER path (ServeDir or embedded), small or large assets. Root: serve/embedded source is byte-identical to the beta tag AND the HTTP dep stack (axum/hyper/tokio/tower-http/mime_guess/rust-embed) is unchanged in Cargo.lock. So there is NO source-level defect to fix. Most likely explanation for the reporter's beta crash: their 'cargo install --path .' ran WITHOUT --locked, so it could resolve a transiently-broken transitive dep version (now gone), and/or a Linux-specific issue (reporter on Linux, verified here on macOS only). CONCLUSION: nothing to fix in code. No fabricated fix. Recommend refile-as-status on dollspace + Linux confirmation rather than a code change.","created_at":"2026-07-29T07:17:08.533201Z","kind":"result"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":71,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T07:25:17.828959Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"a3abff8a-7d9a-44fe-9a11-8e75a232d612","comment_uuid":"4e86a179-34dc-41f0-bb2c-5629c0aac143","author":"anon-8ea7a055","content":"Closed the loop per operator decision (option 2): posted a not-reproducing status comment on forecast-bio/crosslink#654 (issuecomment-5114475221) with the repro evidence (both serve paths, real embedded asset), the source+lockfile-unchanged analysis, the likely cause (cargo install without --locked pulling a transient dep; Linux-unverified), and Claude authorship note. No dollspace issue opened (avoids cluttering with a non-repro), no code change (no source defect). Throwaway worktree removed, no commits. DONE.","created_at":"2026-07-29T07:25:17.828939Z","kind":"result"}}
